      "text": "What oversupply? Even in the lower end ranges that they're focusing on, Chinese pluggable makers like Innolight are still bottlenecked for 70-100mW ranges from ECOC channel checks. \n\nCambridge wouldn't be going out financing suppliers with convertible loans for scarce laser capacity. \n\nSuppliers wouldn't be raising ASPs if there was overcapacity. Also not all CW lasers are the same. China is a ways away from from scaling UHP lasers needed for CPO, which is why there's still premiums given to $LITE, $COHR, $SIVE. \n\n$LITE lasers are sold out into 2029 and they're starting negotiations into 2030.",
